meta {
  name: List a source's documents
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/sources/{{scopeSourceId}}/documents
}

docs {
  What this connector actually learned: uri, title, chunk count, and the labels applying to
  each document. Labels are prefix rules resolved at read time, so a folder tag shows on
  files ingested long after it was set.

  Each document also carries `metadata` — a small connector-supplied JSON blob for UI
  display only, `{}` for every connector that doesn't set it. Azure DevOps stamps
  work_item_type/state/team/sprint/parent_id/changed_date/closed_date there, which is what
  the document browser uses to render TFS work items as an Epic/Feature/Story/Task tree
  (sorted: ongoing items by last-updated desc, then completed items by closed-date desc).
}
